# Conformance evidence

- Follow the user's validation timing and test-file constraints. Design coverage before implementation; execute when authorized.
- Use independently authored synthetic cases, approved specifications, explicit oracle/candidate commands, and isolated environments.
- Record target/candidate digests, contract revision, case IDs, runner/environment, seeds, normalization, tolerances, and outcomes.
- Cover normal, boundary, invalid, stateful, side-effect, concurrency, cancellation, and platform behavior appropriate to scope.
- Count timeout, crash, runner failure, skipped/unsupported, malformed output, mismatch, and pass distinctly.
- Use approved tolerances; never normalize away a mismatch or change thresholds to manufacture a pass.
- Submit minimized behavioral counterexamples for firewall review before implementation feedback.

Example: a timed-out case is inconclusive execution evidence, even if both processes timed out.
